# Checked NaturalDual extension exclusions

The five literal matrices are checked against the actual catalogue operators.
The 432 packed rows are checked against the scalar intertwining equations.
Each of twelve checked XOR combinations forces an entry in a fixed column to
vanish, contradicting the square-one equation. No unknown matrices are enumerated.

Generated by `Certificate/source/generate.py` from the row-combination witnesses
of `ExtensionExclusion/source/diagnostic.py`, whose ATLAS attribution and binary
coordinate conventions are retained unchanged. Source context: James (1973),
Lemma 8.3, as used in Aschbacher–Smith H.12.1(1), printed pp.393–394.
-/

